Banpage Public License
V1 by GameFinders

(C) 2026 GameFinders

everyone is allowed to copy the code excluding any entity the author bans under a file in the Git repo named !BANPAGE.txt.

anyone banned cannot do much about it.

a !BANPAGE.txt includes
  -> Banlist
  -> Whitelist

a whitelisted user can relicense the fork under Banpage Public License' above version; or any license that can be swapped to under 5th title.

for the author, you cannot sue them for:
  1- not providing the file they want
  2- putting you as a blacklisted entity on !BANPAGE.txt

to use the license the author has to:

1- include a blank !BANPAGE.txt in the repo that they can control; as for otherwise the license acts like the WTFPL with author's protection.
2- the Git on Cloud doesn't matter; it can be any Git provider; etc. GitHub, GitLab, HuggingFace Hub, etc., the author can use the license so long as this document sits as "LICENSE" in the Git Repo.

1-- what to call Banpage Public License

the shortened name is intended to be BANPAGEPL.

2-- Disclosures

1) a contributor may or may not touch the !BANPAGE.txt file is entirely the author's discreetion.
2) the author cannot be sued by a entity because it served no purpose for their use. THIS LICENSE DOES NOT GUARANTEE A SINGLE THING ABOUT ANY PRODUCT BEING USEFUL FOR ONE SPECIFIC USE; IF THE AUTHOR HAD MADE A PRODUCT FOR OTHER SPECIFIC USES ONLY.
3) if the author is "banned" from their own project, the license then acts like the WTFPL because the !BANPAGE.txt file is now invalid because a contributor tried to ban the author if the contributor had access to the !BANPAGE.txt file.
4) if a author choses to use this license without !BANPAGE.txt file; they can but then the license acts like the WTFPL.
5) The creator of license may release newer versions of BANPAGEPL.

3-- Licensing terms for when !BANPAGE.txt doesn't exist or is invalidated

you just do what the f*ck you want to, except the author can't be sued by a corporate because they wanted to fork it, and you cannot easily change the license.

4-- Author has the control for

Enforcing !BANPAGE.txt
Creating !BANPAGE.txt
Controlling who can access !BANPAGE.txt

5-- Ditching or changing licenses

if at one version the author choses to ditch the Banpage License, they can swap it out for:

- MIT
- GNU GPLv2/GNU GPLv3
- GNU LGPL
- BSD
- WTFPL
- Unlicense
- ZSH License

for the next releases, or other licenses that aren't listed here; but allows to swapping to other licenses.

The author who used to use it; may at any time swap back to Banpage License.
New authors to use this license are welcome to use this license.
